From f9c552b7544a61eef8f74a502d0a45cdf6f4c467 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:51:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Persist the monetary record after a successful ordinary
 connect.

An optional PersistentMonetaryStore receives one snapshot after the
in-memory block and its per-transaction UTXO commits succeed. If that
commit fails, the UTXO commits are undone newest first and the in-memory
parent is restored, with no new monetary snapshot. Earlier script, cost,
coinbase, mint, and context failures do not write it. This is not
ConnectTip and does not accept a block.
